      "problem": "$\\sqrt[3]{-\\frac{216}{343}}=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we rewrite the fraction under the radical as follows:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[3]{-\\frac{216}{343}}=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{(-216)}{343}}\n$$\n\nThe cube root of a quotient of two numbers is equal to the quotient of the cube roots of the numbers. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{(-216)}{343}} & =\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{-216}}{\\sqrt[3]{343}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-6}{7} \\\\  & =-\\frac{6}{7}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
